      en: "The Turkmen Carpet Museum in Ashgabat houses over 2,000 hand-woven carpets, making it one of the world's largest collections. Founded in 1993, the museum's centerpiece is the world's largest hand-woven carpet, measuring 301 m² and certified by Guinness World Records. The exhibits showcase carpets from the 17th century to present, featuring designs from all major Turkmen tribes. The museum's facade is adorned with traditional carpet patterns. It also serves as a research center for carpet history and preservation. Visitors can watch weavers at work, maintaining centuries-old techniques.",
